## 2026-07-28 - US-019
- Added a unit test runner. New `test-unit` npm script runs
  `npm run build:main && tape test/unit/*.js`, and `npm test` now
  runs it after `standard` and `depcheck`. No new dependency: `tape`
  was already a devDependency and the Babel `build/` output is the
  documented bridge from the ESM renderer sources to CommonJS test
  files.
- Wrote `test/unit/time.js` first, against
  `build/renderer/lib/time.js` -- five real assertions on
  `calculateEta` (both no-op guards, seconds-only, minutes, hours).
  Written before the script existed; the seconds-only case failed on
  the first run (the template literal emits two leading spaces, not
  one) and the expectation was corrected against real behaviour.
- Files changed: `package.json` (scripts), `test/unit/time.js` (new),
  `test/AGENTS.md` (new), `progress.log`, `specs/prd.json`.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - **Only `src/renderer/lib/**` and `src/main/**` are unit testable
    through `build/`.** `build:main` ignores `src/renderer/main.js`,
    `components/`, `controllers/` and `pages/` because Vite owns them,
    so nothing under those four paths can be required from a unit
    test. The platform shim lives in `src/renderer/lib/platform/`, so
    US-020 through US-025 are all in range -- which is presumably why
    the shim was put there.
  - **`test-unit` builds first on purpose.** `npx tape test/unit/*.js`
    on its own silently tests whatever `build/` happens to contain,
    which can be an arbitrarily old copy of `src/`. A stale `build/`
    is why the first run of the new test resolved the module at all
    despite `build/` never having been rebuilt this session.
  - **The integration suite is a pre-existing failure**, promoted to
    the Codebase Patterns section above along with the process-cleanup
    consequence. US-019's "`npm run test-integration` still passes"
    criterion is unsatisfiable as written; it is unchanged by this
    story (verified against stashed HEAD) rather than passing.
  - `test/index.js` requires each integration file by hand, so adding
    `test/unit/` cannot affect the integration run.
