## 2026-07-28 - US-020
- Implemented `src/renderer/lib/platform/ipc-os.js` over `ipcRenderer`.
  Every stub body from US-018 now sends or listens on its real
  channel; the JSDoc surface is unchanged, so `docs/platform-shim.md`
  needed no signature edits. A private `listen(channel, listener,
  options)` helper strips the Electron event object, honours
  `{ once: true }` and returns the unsubscribe closure, so every
  `on*` export resolves to a `() => void`.
  `checkForExternalPlayer` collapses the existing send-then-`once`
  pair into one promise, registering the reply listener before the
  send (today's `media-controller.js` registers it after, which is a
  race the shim closes).
- Test-first: `test/unit/platform-ipc-os.js` was written and shown
  failing 8/10 before any implementation. It stubs `ipcRenderer` via
  `require.cache` and covers send, receive, unsubscribe, `once`, and
  the request/response round trip, plus two structural assertions --
  every export is an `AsyncFunction`, and calling every export touches
  no `wt-*` channel (FR-9).
- No call site was migrated, per the story.
- Verified every channel the module sends on is registered in
  `src/main/`: 22 via `ipcMain.on` in `src/main/ipc.js`, plus
  `ipcReady` (`ipc.js:24`, `once`) and `stateSaved`
  (`src/main/index.js:126`, `once`).
- Files changed: `src/renderer/lib/platform/ipc-os.js`,
  `test/unit/platform-ipc-os.js`, `docs/platform-shim.md`,
  `src/renderer/lib/platform/AGENTS.md`, `test/AGENTS.md`,
  `specs/prd.json`, `progress.log`.
- Gates: `npm run lint` clean, `npm test` 18/18 (13 new), and
  `npx vite build` still succeeds -- the shim is compiled by both
  toolchains, so Babel passing alone would not prove it.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - The `require.cache` stubbing recipe is promoted to Codebase
    Patterns and written up in `test/AGENTS.md`. It is what makes the
    rest of the shim (US-021 through US-025) unit-testable, so keep
    every shim module on a top-level *named* import from `electron`;
    a destructuring `require` binds eagerly and breaks it.
  - The implementation shape US-021 should copy is recorded in
    `src/renderer/lib/platform/AGENTS.md`, not here: one-line exports
    over a shared `listen()` helper.
  - The two structural tests (all-async, no-`wt-*`) are cheap and
    directly encode FR-9/FR-10. Worth repeating verbatim in the
    `ipc-engine.js` tests with the assertion inverted.
  - The app was not launched this session: nothing imports the shim
    yet, so a launch could not exercise the new code and would only
    reproduce the known pre-existing `electron.remote` error.
